                                        "entry_id": "ff5ae873-3495-35ac-a978-9ec2571878e6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An acute contagious disease of the upper airways and lungs, caused by a virus, which rapidly spreads around the world in seasonal epidemics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dea988fd-e7f1-4c00-9c3a-ddc0366859bb",
                                                "sense_id": "a21cafc4-9434-3c70-8d98-b1253d40de76",
                                                "text": "In early 1919 the Board also issued a film, Dr Wise on Influenza, in which a character called 'Brown' spreads the disease by enacting poor behaviours.\nThis did address transport - by boarding a crowded omnibus, \"Brown may be scattering germs throughout the carriage and giving influenza to a number of people\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
